# One `switch` over the members of an enum, and two of its labels are written with a cast: `case Kind.Null as Listed:`. A cast in a checked file is a conversion that is tested, so the label was
# taken for no constant: the switch was cut at it into a switch, a comparison, a switch, a comparison and a switch, and a value of the last piece went through all five.
# The label is a constant that the type of the cast takes, so the conversion has nothing to test: it stays a case. A cast to a type that does not take it is still compared by itself.
# f1 = nameOf . f2 = odd
# -- source: main.ts
